{
  "reviewer": "maintainability",
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "_history_report_to_dict and _bisect_report_to_dict live in schema/cli.py but are exclusively consumed by formatter built-ins via lazy import",
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/protokit/formatters/_builtin_history.py",
      "line": 79,
      "confidence": 0.88,
      "autofix_class": "refactor",
      "owner": "formatter-author",
      "requires_verification": false,
      "pre_existing": false,
      "suggested_fix": "Move _history_report_to_dict and _bisect_report_to_dict out of schema/cli.py and into the formatter layer \u2014 either directly into their respective _builtin_*.py modules or into a new src/protokit/formatters/_serialization.py. Both functions are pure dataclass-to-dict projections with zero dependency on CLI state. Keeping them in schema/cli.py forces formatter built-ins to reach back into a CLI module at call time, inverts the intended dependency direction (formatters should depend on schema.model, not on schema.cli), and couples the JSON wire format to a CLI implementation file. After the move, the lazy-import workarounds in _builtin_history.py:79 and _builtin_bisect.py:73 become plain top-level imports."
    },
    {
      "title": "make_aggregated_testsuite in _junit_xml.py is never called",
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/protokit/formatters/_junit_xml.py",
      "line": 137,
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "autofix_class": "delete",
      "owner": "formatter-author",
      "requires_verification": false,
      "pre_existing": false,
      "suggested_fix": "Delete make_aggregated_testsuite. The HISTORY junit formatter builds aggregated suites by calling make_testsuite and then setting package/id attributes directly (_builtin_history.py lines 112-120), making this helper dead on arrival. Dead helpers in a public-surface utility module attract copy-paste callers who do not notice the live path diverges."
    },
    {
      "title": "_protokit_version is a module-private helper in _builtin_compat.py but is reached via lazy local import by two other built-in modules",
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/protokit/formatters/_builtin_compat.py",
      "line": 228,
      "confidence": 0.82,
      "autofix_class": "refactor",
      "owner": "formatter-author",
      "requires_verification": false,
      "pre_existing": false,
      "suggested_fix": "Move _protokit_version to _sarif_json.py (it is exclusively a SARIF concern) or to a new formatters/_version.py, then import it at the top of each consumer. This eliminates the lazy local imports in _builtin_history.py:136 and _builtin_bisect.py:159, which are present only to break an artificial coupling, and makes the true dependency explicit."
    },
    {
      "title": "_register_builtin private helper is imported into four _builtin_*.py modules, making it callable by any code that imports those modules",
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/protokit/formatters/_registry.py",
      "line": 176,
      "confidence": 0.72,
      "autofix_class": "refactor",
      "owner": "formatter-author",
      "requires_verification": false,
      "pre_existing": false,
      "suggested_fix": "_register_builtin bypasses the guard rails in register_formatter and should never be called by user code. It leaks into the call graph of anyone who imports a _builtin_*.py module. Consider restricting the import to _registry.py internal use and having each _builtin_*.py declare a list of (name, fn, kind) tuples that _registry.py walks at package init time, eliminating the need for _register_builtin to be importable at all."
    },
    {
      "title": "FormatterContext.level stores a re-serialized CLI-flag string computed by the same three-line expression repeated at three call sites in schema/cli.py",
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/protokit/schema/cli.py",
      "line": 642,
      "confidence": 0.68,
      "autofix_class": "refactor",
      "owner": "formatter-author",
      "requires_verification": true,
      "pre_existing": false,
      "suggested_fix": "The expression level.value.lower().replace(\"_\", \"-\") appears at lines 642, 1200, and 1441. Extract it into a helper or into CompatibilityLevel itself (e.g. a cli_name property). Separately, consider whether FormatterContext.level should accept CompatibilityLevel | None directly instead of a pre-serialized string; formatters that need to branch on level currently must pattern-match string literals like \"consumer-safe\" rather than enum members."
    },
    {
      "title": "warnings imported but unused in _registry.py, kept alive only by a sentinel assignment",
