  "residual_risks": [
    "The lazy-import cycle workaround (formatters._builtin_history and _builtin_bisect importing from schema.cli at call time) is functional but invisible to static analysis. A rename or split of schema/cli.py will surface as a runtime AttributeError rather than a test-collection ImportError.",
    "The equal-and-not-verbose short-circuit in message/cli.py prints Messages are equal. directly rather than delegating to the human formatter. The human formatter has its own equal-case rendering path (diff_human lines 134-139) which is never exercised by the CLI on the equal path, creating latent divergence if those two paths are ever expected to converge.",
    "The two-phase load in load_formatter_pack rolls back by deleting keys in _REGISTRY that are not in _BUILTIN_NAMES. If _register_builtin is ever called concurrently with a pack load (impossible today but possible if CLI startup is parallelised), a race window exists where a built-in key is in _REGISTRY but not yet in _BUILTIN_NAMES and would be incorrectly deleted by the rollback."
  ],
  "testing_gaps": [
    "No test exercises load_formatter_pack rollback when a second entry in a multi-entry FORMATTERS list collides with a built-in name after the first entry was successfully committed. The partial-success-then-rollback path in _registry.py:293-305 is untested.",
    "make_aggregated_testsuite in _junit_xml.py has zero test coverage because it is never called; coverage reports show the file as well-covered, masking the dead-code finding.",
    "The entry_ctx FormatterContext constructed inside history_junit (lines 106-116 of _builtin_history.py) is a full 9-field literal that will silently drop any new FormatterContext fields added in future. No test verifies that all ctx fields propagate correctly into per-entry suites."
  ]
}